+      "id": "cd-1-F16",
+      "severity": "must-fix",
+      "check": "assertion",
+      "evidence": "Still open for two checks. Acceptance 4 (MF-11, line 551) says the territory row count is 'written as found, and the plan does not change to match it.' A test that accepts any count asserts nothing. C-4 (line 669) requires N events to arrive 'with margin' and gives no threshold. Fix: state the expected count and the margin as values in a dbt test or a pytest assertion, and state the update step when the real build differs. The state 09 equality of the removed MF-10 test is covered in part by check 4 (see cd-1-F26)."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F17",
+      "severity": "must-fix",
+      "check": "coverage",
+      "evidence": "Still open. Phase 6 TDD note 1 (line 182) asserts that an edit 11 minutes after its window end is absent from mart_edit_window_5min and present in late_events. F06 (lines 808-810) says the 9-minute and 11-minute rows move to transform/tests/test_edit_window_rules.sql. The rows it lists are only the 10-minute and 10-minute-1-second lateness rows. No row checks mart exclusion or late_events membership, and no row checks check_late_count (check 7). Fix: add a row to test_edit_window_rules.sql that a late edit is absent from mart_edit_window_5min and present in late_events, and a row for check_late_count."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F18",
+      "severity": "must-fix",
+      "check": "mutation",
+      "evidence": "Still open. The net_bytes rows (F08, line 811) cover only the NULL case. No row fixes the value of length_new - length_old with both lengths present and non-zero. No row checks the window sum of net_bytes. A sign-flipped mutant (length_old - length_new) and a dropped subtraction both survive. Fix: add a row with length_old 100 and length_new 40 that expects net_bytes -60, and a window row that sums two such edits."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F19",
+      "severity": "must-fix",
+      "check": "mutation",
+      "evidence": "Still open. The money rows (line 127, and line 422 of the MF-7 text) use '-0.10' as the only value in the sum. A float-sum mutant gives the same result on one value and survives. Fix: add a sum row where float addition drifts, for example 0.10 and 0.20, or ten values of 0.10 that must sum to exactly 1.00."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F20",
+      "severity": "must-fix",
+      "check": "mutation",
+      "evidence": "Still open. The UTC rule (line 31, and F07 at line 810) has rows only at HH:MM:00, HH:MM:04:59 and HH:MM:05:00 in the CI zone. No row would differ under a local time zone, so a mutant that buckets in local time passes on a UTC runner. Fix: add a row whose input is near midnight UTC, or has an explicit non-UTC offset, and state that the test sets the session zone to a non-UTC value."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F21",
+      "severity": "must-fix",
+      "check": "assertion",
+      "evidence": "Still open. The name S3 has two meanings. MF-6 (line 359) says S3 is 'delete out/marts.prev if it exists'. N-5 (line 462) says tests/test_publish_states.py 'gains S3: a failure after the first swap rename'. A test named S3 can assert either behavior. Fix: rename the N-5 case (for example S4) and list it under MF-6 with its own step."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F23",
+      "severity": "note",
+      "check": "coverage",
+      "evidence": "Acceptance 4 (line 79) requires checks 1 to 7 from oracle_map.yml to return a value. No test runs the oracle_map SQL. The check views check_edits_replay_hour, check_top_windows_en and check_late_count (line 178) have no row. 'Returns a value' is not an assertion. Consider one parametrized test that runs each oracle_map query on the fixture warehouse and asserts the expected value."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F24",
+      "severity": "note",
+      "check": "coverage",
+      "evidence": "The COPY ORDER BY rule for byte-identical marts (N-2, line 461) has no test row. Acceptance 2 checks it only on the full real build, with sha256sum, so a failure surfaces late. Consider a row in tests/test_publish_states.py or a dbt test that runs the publish COPY twice on the fixture."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F25",
+      "severity": "note",
+      "check": "dry",
+      "evidence": "Phase 5 TDD note 3 (line 166) says 'a dedup test' and names no file. The in-connection dedup row should be a parametrize row in tests/test_stream_resume.py, as F03 does for the restart case. The revision ledger row cd-1-F01 (line 841) still verifies by grep, which MF-4 replaced with a test."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "cd-1-F26",
+      "severity": "note",
+      "check": "coverage",
+      "evidence": "New. The real-build state 09 equality (MF-10) lived in transform/tests/test_connecticut_planning_region.sql, which F02 (line 781) replaces with transform/tests/test_place_county_unknown.sql. F02 does not list the equality. Check 4 (Phase 4, line 143, and Acceptance 4) still compares county sums with state sums, and the UNKNOWN county is in that sum, so Connecticut is covered in part. Fix: add the state 09 equality row to test_place_county_unknown.sql or to the check 4 test."
+    },
